Recommends: nftables, unattended-upgrades
Description: Self-hosted web hosting panel for a VPS
 Forja manages several isolated websites (Node, PHP, Python, static or
 Dockerfile) on a single VPS and publishes them through Cloudflare tunnels,
 so no inbound port has to be opened.
 .
 It has two roles: administrator (sees everything) and client (only their own
 accounts). The package ships the privileged agent (forja-agent, runs as root
 and listens only on a Unix socket), the unprivileged panel API and the web
 interface, plus the systemd units and the container/Caddy drop-ins they need.
 .
 Note: Cloudflare DNS-01 certificates need a Caddy build that includes the
 caddy-dns/cloudflare module; the stock Debian caddy package does not.
